@meta
id: 19-01
title: Every hit in the tree
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: vimgrep
par: 55
minutes: 5
vscode: Ctrl+Shift+F, type the name, click the one result
open: README.md

@brief
The README says refunds go through `PaymentService.sendRefund`. The
method was called `refund` until last sprint, and one caller somewhere
under `src/` was missed by the rename and still calls `refund(` on the
payment service. Nothing tells you which file.

In VS Code you would press Ctrl+Shift+F, type the name, and click the
result. Vim has the same search, and it puts the results somewhere more
useful than a sidebar. `:vimgrep /pattern/ **/*.ts` searches every
TypeScript file under the current directory, collects every match into
the quickfix list, and jumps to the first one. The quickfix list is a
list of places: file, line, column, and the text found there. The rest
of this chapter is about what you can do with such a list. For now you
need one thing from it: when there is exactly one hit, `:vimgrep` takes
you straight to it.

Find the stale call and change it to `sendRefund`. The README mentions
the old name too and stays as it is: it is not a TypeScript file, so the
glob never opens it.

@keys
| `:vimgrep /pattern/ **/*.ts` | search every .ts file under the tree, jump to the first hit |
| `:vim` | the same command, abbreviated |
| `**` | any depth of directories |

@hints
The pattern is a vim regex, the same dialect as `/` and `:s`. You want a
call to `.refund(` and nothing else, so the dot has to be escaped or it
matches any character, and `sendRefund(` would be a hit too.
--
`:vimgrep /\.refund(/ **/*.ts` and Enter. One hit, so vim opens the file
and puts the cursor on the match.
--
The cursor lands on the dot, which is where the match starts. `w` moves
onto `refund`; `ciw` changes the word. `:wq` from there.

@solution
    :vimgrep /\.refund(/ **/*.ts<Enter>  w ciw sendRefund <Esc> :wq<Enter>

`:vimgrep` is search across files, and it puts what it finds where it
can be acted on rather than looked at. The glob after the pattern says
which files: `**/*.ts` is every TypeScript file at any depth below the
directory vim was started in, which here is the project root.
`src/**/*.ts` would narrow it to `src`; `*.ts` would be the top level
only. `:vim` is accepted as an abbreviation and is what people type.

The cursor lands on the first character of the match, which for the
pattern `\.refund(` is the dot. That is why there is a `w` in the
solution: a pattern that starts one character left of the word you want
lands you one character left of it. `/refund(/` would have landed on
the `r`, but it also matches `sendRefund(`, and the escaped dot was
there to rule that out. Pattern precision and landing position trade
off, and `w` is cheap.

When there are many hits the list holds all of them. That is the next
lesson.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund` (it was
`refund` until last sprint), which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  placedAt: Date;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).sendRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@start src/domain/order/order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      placedAt: record.placedAt,
    };
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@start src/domain/payment/payment.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PaymentRepository } from './payment.repository';
import { PaymentProducer } from './payment.producer';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class PaymentProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(PaymentRepository) protected paymentRepository: PaymentRepository,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async reverse(id: string) {
    const payment = await this.paymentRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!payment) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const receipt = await this.paymentService.refund(payment.orderId);

    await this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: id, receipt });

    return receipt;
  }
}

@expected src/domain/payment/payment.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PaymentRepository } from './payment.repository';
import { PaymentProducer } from './payment.producer';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class PaymentProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(PaymentRepository) protected paymentRepository: PaymentRepository,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async reverse(id: string) {
    const payment = await this.paymentRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!payment) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const receipt = await this.paymentService.sendRefund(payment.orderId);

    await this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: id, receipt });

    return receipt;
  }
}

@start src/domain/payment/payment.producer.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { Channel } from '../../infrastructure/rabbit/channel';

type RefundIssuedEvent = {
  paymentId: string;
  receipt: string;
};

@injectable()
export class PaymentProducer {
  constructor(@inject(Channel) protected channel: Channel) {}

  public async refundIssued(event: RefundIssuedEvent) {
    await this.channel.publish('payments', 'payment.sendRefund', event);
  }
}

@start src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async sendRefund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post('/sendRefund', { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}
